  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 103 AM EDT Tue Oct 20 2026\n\nAs we head towards the end of the work week, heights continue to \nfall across the region and eventually an upper level low will form \nin the vicinity of Cuba over the weekend. Wrap around moisture will \nincrease rain chances, especially across the east coast metro. In \naddition to the higher rain chances, the pressure gradient will \ntighten once again as strong high pressure builds into New England. \nExpect breezy NE winds this weekend into early next week, with early \nindications of wind gusts of 30-40 mph possible, especially along \nthe coast. \n\nHigh temperatures during the extended period will be fairly \nconsistent, ranging from the low to middle 80s each day. Overnight \ntemps will be in the 60s/70s.",
